From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:06:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: t8132: Refuse a call to a powered-down
 DCP without failing the session

A call that reaches a DCP while it is powered down fails the whole
retained session. This covers both the power-down after a blank and the
one for a sleep. The CPU is stopped, so RTKit refuses the message
("Endpoint 0x37 is not running"). The session is then quarantined and
the panel stays dark until a reboot. Nothing about the firmware was
lost: the message was simply never sent.

Refuse such a call at the start of the call path with -EAGAIN and a
ratelimited warning, and leave the session alone. The colour and
timing paths already keep their state for the power-up; this is the
net for any path that does not. Every power-up clears gated before it
makes its own calls, and the power-downs make theirs before they set
it.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 28480b18ca..9d26f22568 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -3154,6 +3154,17 @@ static int dcp_m4_runtime_call_stream(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r, unsigned int met
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * Powered down (after a blank or for a sleep): the CPU is stopped and its
+	 * DARTs may be off, so nothing can be sent. Refuse this call alone, without
+	 * failing the session; the caller keeps its state for the power-up. Every
+	 * power-up clears gated before its own calls.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(dcp->gated))) {
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(dcp->dev, "A%03u not sent: display coprocessor powered down\n",
+				     method);
+		return -EAGAIN;
+	}
 	/* The epoch our own call goes out in, for its nested callbacks. */
 	if (!remote) {
 		r->ext_local_calls++;
-- 
2.43.0

